UPDATE pages SET
    content_html = '<h2>Who We Are</h2><p>Trader Gulf is an independent forex broker review and comparison platform for traders across the Middle East, North Africa, and beyond. We are not a broker and we do not handle client funds. Our mission is to provide transparent, unbiased information so you can find the right broker for your needs.</p><h2>Our Methodology</h2><p>Every broker we review undergoes a structured evaluation process covering:</p><ul><li><strong>Regulation and safety</strong> — We verify regulatory status directly with the issuing authority (FCA, ASIC, CySEC, DFSA).</li><li><strong>Trading costs</strong> — We measure real spreads during live market hours, not just advertised minimums.</li><li><strong>Platform quality</strong> — We test MT4, MT5, cTrader, and proprietary platforms on desktop and mobile.</li><li><strong>Deposit and withdrawal</strong> — We evaluate speed, reliability, and available methods for MENA region traders.</li><li><strong>Customer support</strong> — We contact support teams via live chat and email to assess quality and response time.</li><li><strong>Islamic account conditions</strong> — We review swap-free account structures for genuine Sharia compliance.</li></ul><h2>Our Commitment to Independence</h2><p>Some brokers featured on Trader Gulf pay us a referral commission when you open an account through our links. This <strong>never influences our ratings or editorial content</strong>. Brokers cannot pay for higher ratings. Our editorial team determines all scores using objective, criteria-based evaluation.</p><h2>Who We Write For</h2><p>We write for traders of all experience levels across the MENA region — from first-time demo traders to experienced professionals. We place particular emphasis on:</p><ul><li>Islamic (swap-free) account availability for Muslim traders</li><li>Brokers with Arabic-language platform and support</li><li>Deposit and withdrawal methods accessible from Lebanon, UAE, Saudi Arabia, Egypt, and Kuwait</li><li>Regulatory credentials and fund safety for non-EU clients</li></ul><h2>Contact Us</h2><p>Questions, corrections, or broker review requests? Reach us at <a href="mailto:info@tradergulf.com">info@tradergulf.com</a>. We respond to all enquiries within 48 hours.</p>',
    meta_title = 'About Trader Gulf | Independent Forex Broker Reviews',
    meta_description = 'Trader Gulf provides independent, unbiased forex broker reviews and comparisons for traders across the Middle East and North Africa. Learn about our methodology.'
WHERE slug = 'about';

UPDATE pages SET
    content_html = '<p><em>Last updated: August 2025</em></p><h2>1. Who We Are</h2><p>Trader Gulf ("we", "our", "us") operates tradergulf.com, an independent forex broker review and comparison website. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your personal data when you visit our site.</p><h2>2. Information We Collect</h2><p>We may collect the following types of information:</p><ul><li><strong>Usage data:</strong> Pages visited, time on site, referring URL, browser type, device type, and IP address — collected automatically via server logs and analytics tools.</li><li><strong>Cookie data:</strong> We use cookies for analytics and to store your cookie consent preference. See section 5 for details.</li><li><strong>Contact information:</strong> If you email us, we retain your email address and message solely to respond to your enquiry.</li></ul><h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2><p>We use collected data to improve the content and performance of tradergulf.com, understand how users navigate the site, respond to enquiries, and monitor site security. We do not sell, rent, or share your personal data with third parties for marketing purposes.</p><h2>4. Third-Party Links and Affiliate Disclosure</h2><p>Our site contains links to external broker websites. When you follow these links, you are subject to the destination site\'s privacy policy. Some of these are affiliate links — if you register with a broker through our link, we may receive a commission. This does not affect the price you pay or our editorial independence.</p><h2>5. Cookies</h2><p>We use essential cookies (required for the site to function) and analytics cookies (Google Analytics, with anonymised IPs) to understand visitor behaviour. You can control cookies through your browser settings. Declining analytics cookies does not affect your use of the site.</p><h2>6. Data Retention</h2><p>Server logs are retained for up to 90 days. Analytics data is retained per Google Analytics\'s standard retention policies.</p><h2>7. Your Rights</h2><p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights to access, correct, or delete your personal data. Contact us at <a href="mailto:info@tradergulf.com">info@tradergulf.com</a> to exercise these rights.</p><h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2><p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of this page reflects the latest revision. Continued use of the site constitutes acceptance of any changes.</p>',
    meta_title = 'Privacy Policy | Trader Gulf',
    meta_description = 'Read the Trader Gulf privacy policy. We explain how we collect, use, and protect your personal data when you use our forex broker comparison website.'
WHERE slug = 'privacy-policy';

UPDATE pages SET
    content_html = '<div style="background:#fef2f2;border:1px solid #fca5a5;border-radius:8px;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;margin-bottom:2rem"><strong>Risk Warning:</strong> Trading forex and CFDs involves significant risk of loss and is not suitable for all investors. The majority of retail trader accounts lose money. You should never trade with money you cannot afford to lose.</div><h2>High Risk Investment Warning</h2><p>Forex (foreign exchange) and CFD (contract for difference) trading are complex leveraged financial instruments that carry a high risk of capital loss. Leverage amplifies both gains and losses, meaning you can lose more than your initial deposit in some account types.</p><p>Statistics from regulated brokers consistently show that between 70% and 89% of retail CFD trading accounts are unprofitable. This figure varies by broker and market conditions but reflects the inherent difficulty of consistently profiting from short-term speculation.</p><h2>Not Investment Advice</h2><p>All content on tradergulf.com — including broker reviews, ratings, comparisons, articles, guides, tools, and calculators — is provided for <strong>informational and educational purposes only</strong>. Nothing on this website constitutes investment advice, financial advice, or a recommendation to buy, sell, or hold any financial instrument or security.</p><p>You should seek independent financial or investment advice from a qualified professional before making any trading decisions. Ensure that any trading activity is appropriate for your personal financial situation, investment objectives, and risk tolerance.</p><h2>Affiliate Disclosure</h2><p>Trader Gulf maintains commercial relationships with some of the brokers featured on this site. We may receive a referral fee or commission when you open an account through a link on our website. This compensation <strong>does not influence our editorial independence, broker ratings, or review content</strong>. All evaluations are conducted using objective, criteria-based methodology by our editorial team.</p><h2>Regulatory Disclaimer</h2><p>Trader Gulf is a comparison and information website only. We are not authorised or regulated by any financial authority to provide investment advice or brokerage services. Before opening any trading account, always verify that the broker is properly regulated and authorised to serve clients in your jurisdiction.</p><h2>Accuracy of Information</h2><p>We make every effort to ensure that broker spreads, fees, regulatory status, and other details are accurate and current. However, trading conditions and regulatory statuses change frequently. We cannot guarantee the accuracy of all information at all times. Always verify current terms and conditions directly with the relevant broker before trading.</p><h2>Jurisdictional Notice</h2><p>Forex and CFD trading may be restricted or regulated differently in various countries and jurisdictions. It is your sole responsibility to ensure you comply with all applicable laws and regulations in your country of residence before engaging in any forex or CFD trading activity.</p>',
    meta_title = 'Risk Disclaimer | Trader Gulf',
    meta_description = 'Important risk disclaimer for tradergulf.com. Forex and CFD trading carries significant risk of loss. Read before acting on any information on this site.'
WHERE slug = 'risk-disclaimer';

